  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas goes through a reversible cycle <math><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>d</mi></math> has the V - T diagram shown below. Process <math><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>c</mi></math> are adiabatic.<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0179_0637a02f7a06.png\" style=\"width: 257px; height: 183px;\" /><br /><br />The corresponding P - V diagram for the process is (all figures are schematic and not drawn to scale) :"
  },
